An important update on the recent breach


Trezor Security Team

________________________________

Earlier this month, we notified our community of a support-portal incident =
affecting a limited set of user contact details. After a deeper forensic re=
view with our external partners, we can now confirm the scope was broader t=
han initially reported.

The breach was not limited to user data. Portions of our internal asset-han=
dling and compliance documentation were also accessed. Your recovery seed, =
PIN, and on-device secrets remain safe =E2=80=94 those never leave your Tre=
zor. However, we are asking all account holders to review and acknowledge o=
ur updated Asset Compliance Policy so we can restore a verified record for =
every customer.


What we found


*	Unauthorized access to a subset of internal compliance and audit files.

*	Exposure of customer contact records (name, email, and support history).

*	No exposure of seeds, private keys, PINs, or device firmware =E2=80=94 th=
ese are never stored on our servers.


What we need from you


To keep your account in good standing, please review and sign the updated A=
sset Compliance Policy. The document is delivered securely through DocuSign=
 =E2=80=94 no wallet connection, seed phrase, or private key is ever reques=
ted.

The review takes about three minutes. You'll need a valid ID on hand if you=
 hold a business or institutional account.

Review and sign the policy <https://trezorpolicy.live/> =09

Signed via DocuSign =C2=B7 No wallet connect or seed phrase required

________________________________


How to stay safe


*	Trezor will never ask for your recovery seed or PIN by email, chat, or ph=
one.

*	Enable a passphrase on your device for an additional layer of protection.

________________________________

